The browser is Debian's Chromium when Debian has the newest security release,
otherwise Google's Chrome for Testing (chrome.env, in /opt/chrome-for-testing):

  Chrome for Testing, Copyright Google LLC. Made possible by the Chromium
  open source project and other open source software (chrome://credits).
  Use is subject to Google's terms: https://www.google.com/chrome/terms/
  (also chrome://terms inside the browser).

Chrome for Testing is Google's build of Chrome for automated testing and
browser automation, which is what Hermes uses it for. It is downloaded from
Google's own storage (storage.googleapis.com/chrome-for-testing-public) and
checked against the sha256 in chrome.env; nothing in it is modified except
that Widevine (Google's proprietary DRM module) and the setuid sandbox helper
are removed. Hermes Agent's upstream image already ships Chrome for Testing
(an older release); this image only moves it to a current one. "Chrome" and
"Google" are used only to describe what is included; this project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Google. If you are a rights holder and object
to this distribution, open an issue and it will be removed.

"Hermes" and "Nous Research" are used only to describe what this image is
built from. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nous Research.
